# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# This file holds no secrets, because everything Vite puts in the browser bundle
# is public by definition — anyone can read it in devtools.
#
# Locally the backend runs on port 5000, so this is the default and you can skip
# the file entirely while developing.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:5000

# On Vercel: set VITE_API_URL in the *frontend* project's environment variables
# to the deployed backend URL (https://<backend-project>.vercel.app).
#
# Two things about this that are easy to lose an afternoon to:
#
# 1. Vite substitutes env vars at BUILD time, not at runtime. The value is
#    compiled into the JavaScript bundle, so setting it in the dashboard is not
#    enough — you have to redeploy the frontend afterwards, or the live bundle
#    keeps pointing at whatever was there when it was built.
# 2. Only VITE_-prefixed vars reach the browser. A backend-only secret named
#    without that prefix is invisible to the frontend (which is the point), and
#    one named WITH it would be shipped to every visitor.
